# What never belongs in the web image's build context.
#
# Without this file `COPY . .` in the build stage copies the host's
# node_modules *over* the one the deps stage just installed — and a Windows or
# macOS install of @next/swc or esbuild is a native binary that cannot run in
# an Alpine container. The build then fails for a reason that reads nothing
# like "your build context was wrong".
#
# It is also the difference between sending a few megabytes to the daemon and
# sending a few hundred.

# Installed inside the image by the deps stage, from package-lock.json.
node_modules
.pnpm-store

# Build output. Produced in the image; a stale host copy would be baked in.
.next
out
*.tsbuildinfo

# Local-only configuration. The runtime reads MRIP_API_URL from the
# environment, so a developer's .env.local must not travel into an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Version control and editor state.
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea

# Nothing the server loads at runtime.
README.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
coverage
.eslintcache
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
